s clay gives it muscle and grip, but the modern polish keeps the tannins plush rather than rustic.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:85,287:60,288:88,289:85,290:88,291:72,292:0,293:22,13:85,12:70,15:50,14:45,16:20,135:50,130:20,126:35,159:55,142:50,140:35,167:45,168:35,156:40,157:45,158:25,186:30,151:20,213:55,216:50,226:40,237:75,238:60,255:80,247:60,245:85,259:75,282:95,279:60,294:100,295:100,297:100,315:100"},{"s":"chateau-cantemerle-haut-medoc","n":"Château Cantemerle","p":"Château Cantemerle","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Haut-Médoc","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Merlot","Cabernet Franc","Petit Verdot"],"pr":40,"abv":13.5,"e":"12 months in French oak, about 40% new","sv":"16–18°C","d":"30–60 minutes","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"A fifth growth that drinks like an insider''s secret: red and black currants, cedar and a whisper of tobacco leaf on a medium-weight, gracefully built frame. Classic claret proportions at a price that makes cellaring a case painless.","x":"284:2,285:62,286:62,287:52,288:62,289:62,290:62,291:45,292:0,293:25,13:75,6:45,1:40,14:35,9:30,159:55,163:35,142:30,119:30,93:30,71:25,140:25,148:15,156:20,214:55,231:45,236:75,240:55,258:80,256:40,245:50,259:30,260:20,282:60,280:35,283:30,295:100,298:100,294:100,301:100"},{"s":"chateau-greysac-medoc","n":"Château Greysac","p":"Château Greysac","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Médoc","g":["Merlot","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Franc","Petit Verdot"],"pr":20,"abv":13,"e":"12 months in French oak, about a third new","sv":"15–17°C","d":"Optional; 30 minutes helps","w":"Now–10 years from vintage","ds":"Everyday Médoc in the old style: plum and blackcurrant with a dusty, gravelly edge, a little cedar and a savory leafiness. Medium-bodied and honest, it is the bottle for a Tuesday steak frites rather than a vertical tasting.","x":"284:2,285:58,286:55,287:50,288:55,289:50,290:48,291:30,292:0,293:30,13:60,9:55,14:45,6:35,159:45,88:20,119:30,153:35,140:20,151:25,156:15,217:50,218:20,231:40,258:75,242:50,256:60,246:30,260:25,259:15,283:65,280:30,302:100,294:100,301:100,315:100"},{"s":"chateau-cheval-blanc-saint-emilion","n":"Château Cheval Blanc","p":"Château Cheval Blanc","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Saint-Émilion Grand Cru","g":["Cabernet Franc","Merlot"],"pr":750,"abv":14,"e":"18 months in new French oak","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2 hours when young","w":"12–50 years from vintage","ds":"Cabernet Franc at its most aristocratic, grown on the gravel and clay that border Pomerol: black cherry, mulberry and violet with a cool streak of mint and licorice. Velvet-textured yet weightless on the finish, it gains truffle and cigar over decades.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:75,287:62,288:82,289:88,290:95,291:60,292:0,293:25,14:75,15:55,3:50,17:40,16:30,71:60,81:40,97:35,99:25,126:40,159:40,142:35,150:30,148:20,186:30,168:30,157:30,156:25,213:70,212:60,226:50,236:80,252:75,248:90,238:55,255:70,259:60,282:95,279:45,295:100,299:100,310:100,297:100"},{"s":"vieux-chateau-certan-pomerol","n":"Vieux Château Certan","p":"Vieux Château Certan","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Pomerol","g":["Merlot","Cabernet Franc","Cabernet Sauvignon"],"pr":350,"abv":14,"e":"18–22 months in French oak, mostly new","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1–2 hours when young","w":"10–40 years from vintage","ds":"Pomerol''s most Médoc-minded estate: black cherry and plum on a deep bed of iron-rich clay, truffle and cocoa, with Cabernet Franc adding lift and line. Velvet-textured but never soft, it pairs Right Bank sensuality with real architecture.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:72,287:60,288:80,289:82,290:90,291:60,292:0,293:25,14:80,15:70,12:45,9:40,3:30,71:45,150:55,143:50,152:40,148:25,126:30,159:40,142:30,170:35,167:30,157:25,186:30,213:80,212:45,226:50,236:70,248:85,242:45,245:60,259:55,282:95,279:45,299:100,295:100,310:100,297:100"},{"s":"chateau-cap-de-faugeres-castillon","n":"Château Cap de Faugères","p":"Château Cap de Faugères","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Castillon Côtes de Bordeaux","g":["Merlot","Cabernet Franc","Cabernet Sauvignon"],"pr":22,"abv":14,"e":"12 months in French oak, partly new","sv":"16–17°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–10 years from vintage","ds":"Right Bank generosity on a budget from the limestone slopes just east of Saint-Émilion: ripe black plum and cherry, a lick of mocha and a soft, rounded palate. Plush and immediately giving, it delivers Merlot comfort without the Pomerol price.","x":"284:3,285:52,286:55,287:62,288:68,289:65,290:55,291:45,292:0,293:20,15:75,14:65,12:45,9:30,28:20,167:35,170:30,156:35,157:30,126:25,151:25,152:25,159:20,213:55,226:55,224:50,241:60,250:65,244:60,256:70,259:30,283:60,279:40,302:100,294:100,314:100,300:100"},{"s":"chateau-haut-bailly-pessac-leognan","n":"Château Haut-Bailly","p":"Château Haut-Bailly","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Pessac-Léognan","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Merlot","Cabernet Franc","Petit Verdot"],"pr":160,"abv":13.5,"e":"16 months in French oak, 50–65% new","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1–2 hours when young","w":"10–35 years from vintage","ds":"Graves at its silkiest: cassis and black cherry threaded with the warm-gravel smokiness and pipe tobacco that mark Pessac-Léognan. Haut-Bailly prizes finesse over force, and its tannins are among the most caressing in Bordeaux.","x":"284:2,285:62,286:72,287:55,288:72,289:78,290:85,291:55,292:0,293:25,13:75,14:55,6:35,9:30,3:25,158:55,140:60,142:40,186:50,187:40,159:50,71:30,81:20,148:25,150:15,143:20,156:20,212:80,214:60,236:90,248:70,242:50,258:80,249:55,259:50,282:90,279:45,295:100,299:100,310:100,297:100"},{"s":"chateau-carbonnieux-blanc-pessac-leognan","n":"Château Carbonnieux Blanc","p":"Château Carbonnieux","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Pessac-Léognan","g":["Sauvignon Blanc","Sémillon"],"pr":45,"abv":13,"e":"10 months on lees in French oak, about a third new","sv":"10–12°C","d":"Not needed; 20 minutes in a carafe opens it","w":"Now–12 years from vintage","ds":"White Graves in its classic form: grapefruit and lemon from Sauvignon, a waxy, quietly honeyed breadth from Sémillon, and a gentle toast from lees-stirred barrels. Brisk and stony, yet with enough substance to stand up to a cream sauce.","x":"284:3,285:72,286:3,287:52,288:60,289:65,290:68,291:40,292:0,293:20,36:65,34:55,40:40,66:35,53:40,49:35,89:25,94:20,85:35,73:25,193:25,136:45,137:30,140:25,157:25,156:15,177:25,222:40,228:55,224:30,240:75,236:65,258:75,266:40,259:30,279:60,282:45,303:100,305:100,318:100,298:100"},{"s":"chateau-bonnet-blanc-entre-deux-mers","n":"Château Bonnet Blanc","p":"André Lurton","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Entre-Deux-Mers","g":["Sauvignon Blanc","Sémillon","Muscadelle"],"pr":14,"abv":12,"e":"Stainless steel with brief lees contact","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Within 2 years of release","ds":"The house white of half the bistros in Bordeaux: zesty grapefruit, lime and fresh-cut grass with a lick of elderflower. Light, snappy and unoaked, it does exactly one job and does it beautifully alongside a plate of oysters.","x":"284:3,285:70,286:1,287:40,288:35,289:50,290:42,291:0,292:0,293:10,36:65,34:50,35:45,66:40,46:45,60:20,89:45,94:25,76:30,85:25,136:30,141:15,228:75,225:35,229:40,240:90,256:75,261:90,279:85,283:80,306:100,303:100,318:100,313:100,323:100"},{"s":"chateau-d-yquem-sauternes","n":"Château d''Yquem","p":"Château d''Yquem","t":"dessert","c":"France","r":"Bordeaux","a":"Sauternes","g":["Sémillon","Sauvignon Blanc"],"pr":450,"abv":14,"e":"About 20 months in new French oak","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed; 30 minutes in the glass is enough","w":"Now–100 years from vintage","ds":"The reference point for noble rot: apricot, pineapple and candied orange steeped in honey and saffron, with a satin, almost oily texture. What sets it apart is the acidity that keeps all that richness in motion, carrying a finish that seems to go on for minutes.","x":"284:90,285:72,286:5,287:60,288:95,289:95,290:100,291:60,292:0,293:25,55:75,32:50,58:50,59:45,31:50,39:50,210:60,43:30,192:8