lanc"],"pr":140,"abv":13.5,"e":"About 12 months in barrels and 320-litre ''cigares'', a portion new","sv":"10–12°C","d":"30–60 minutes when young","w":"3–20 years from vintage","ds":"Sauvignon Blanc rebuilt as a grand vin: grapefruit, lime and white peach set off by a blast of gunflint and struck-match reduction. Dense and laser-focused, it reveals the silex soils of Saint-Andelain with uncommon intensity and ages like fine white Burgundy.","x":"284:2,285:88,286:2,287:60,288:62,289:85,290:90,291:30,292:0,293:20,36:60,35:50,40:45,53:40,66:35,60:30,49:25,137:90,147:55,158:50,136:60,138:40,141:40,85:25,100:15,157:15,177:20,230:75,223:25,249:90,255:75,243:95,248:80,237:45,268:60,259:25,282:85,279:60,305:100,303:100,318:100,307:100"},{"s":"domaine-champalou-vouvray","n":"Vouvray","p":"Domaine Champalou","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Vouvray","g":["Chenin Blanc"],"pr":24,"abv":12.5,"e":"Fermented in tank and older barrels; aged on fine lees","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–10 years from vintage","ds":"A sec-tendre Vouvray that captures Chenin''s charm: quince, yellow apple and pear with honeysuckle and chamomile over a chalky core. A touch of richness rounds the edges while bright acidity keeps it tasting dry and lively.","x":"284:12,285:82,286:2,287:45,288:50,289:62,290:62,291:10,292:0,293:15,51:60,47:55,49:50,34:45,53:30,74:40,73:35,79:30,192:20,193:25,194:15,138:55,136:35,129:10,222:45,229:50,228:45,240:75,256:55,236:50,260:30,266:30,279:70,282:45,296:100,298:100,318:100,308:100"},{"s":"domaine-huet-le-mont-vouvray-demi-sec","n":"Le Mont Vouvray Demi-Sec","p":"Domaine Huet","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Vouvray","g":["Chenin Blanc"],"pr":48,"abv":13,"e":"Fermented and aged in old demi-muids, foudres and stainless steel","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed young; 30 minutes for mature bottles","w":"Now–40 years from vintage","ds":"From flinty clay over limestone, Le Mont is Huet''s most chiseled site: quince, yellow apple and lemon curd edged with beeswax and linden. The residual sugar reads as texture rather than sweetness, held in tension by electric acidity, and it ages for decades into honey and lanolin.","x":"284:32,285:90,286:2,287:50,288:55,289:75,290:85,291:5,292:0,293:18,51:75,47:50,49:45,53:35,55:30,43:35,192:50,193:40,194:30,73:40,79:30,86:30,129:20,138:50,137:35,136:40,222:60,230:60,229:50,249:75,243:75,248:70,258:85,260:50,282:100,279:55,296:100,308:100,322:100,298:100"},{"s":"domaine-du-clos-naudin-vouvray-brut-reserve","n":"Vouvray Brut Réserve","p":"Domaine du Clos Naudin","t":"sparkling","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Vouvray","g":["Chenin Blanc"],"pr":38,"abv":12.5,"e":"Traditional method; several years on lees in tufa cellars, low dosage","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–10 years from release","ds":"Philippe Foreau''s sparkling Vouvray uses Chenin''s natural acidity to great effect: quince, green apple and lemon over chalk, framed by brioche from long lees ageing. The mousse is fine and persistent, and the finish carries a quiet honeyed note.","x":"284:6,285:85,286:1,287:45,288:45,289:62,290:68,291:5,292:90,293:30,51:55,46:50,47:40,49:40,34:50,40:35,74:30,73:25,79:20,192:20,193:20,178:35,180:30,181:25,138:60,136:30,233:60,228:65,222:30,240:85,249:60,236:60,243:55,272:100,266:40,283:55,280:35,323:100,305:100,319:100,318:100"},{"s":"nicolas-joly-clos-de-la-coulee-de-serrant","n":"Clos de la Coulée de Serrant","p":"Nicolas Joly","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Savennières-Coulée de Serrant","g":["Chenin Blanc"],"pr":150,"abv":14.5,"e":"Native-yeast fermentation in old 500-litre barrels; biodynamic, minimal sulfur","sv":"12–14°C","d":"2–4 hours, even when mature","w":"5–30 years from vintage","ds":"Biodynamic Chenin from a single monopole of steep schist above the Loire: quince, baked apple and chamomile with beeswax, almond and a deliberately oxidative edge. Powerful, dry and gripping, it can seem severe on opening and keeps transforming in the glass over days.","x":"284:4,285:82,286:4,287:72,288:80,289:80,290:88,291:15,292:0,293:30,51:75,47:45,33:40,55:35,32:25,39:35,79:45,86:30,192:50,193:60,194:35,202:30,203:20,129:20,132:20,136:50,139:40,141:30,222:80,223:45,232:35,237:70,248:85,253:40,242:50,239:40,267:45,265:85,260:50,282:95,280:40,298:100,296:100,303:100,310:100,315:100"},{"s":"domaine-de-la-pepiere-muscadet-sevre-et-maine-sur-lie","n":"Muscadet Sèvre et Maine Sur Lie","p":"Domaine de la Pépière","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Muscadet Sèvre et Maine","g":["Melon de Bourgogne"],"pr":18,"abv":12,"e":"Native-yeast fermentation; aged on lees in underground glass-lined tanks until bottling","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–8 years from vintage","ds":"Muscadet as it should taste: lemon and green apple over a briny, crushed-shell salinity, with a faint leesy breadiness and a prickle of freshness. Lean, bone-dry and quietly serious, it might as well have been designed for the oyster bed.","x":"284:1,285:85,286:1,287:30,288:30,289:50,290:55,291:0,292:3,293:12,34:60,35:45,46:55,49:30,69:20,85:20,141:85,144:75,136:60,137:25,181:30,179:25,228:85,225:60,230:45,240:95,243:80,249:55,258:75,266:90,261:90,265:30,279:80,306:100,305:100,303:100,307:100"},{"s":"charles-joguet-chinon-clos-de-la-dioterie","n":"Chinon Clos de la Dioterie","p":"Charles Joguet","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Chinon","g":["Cabernet Franc"],"pr":50,"abv":13,"e":"12–15 months in older French barrels","sv":"15–17°C","d":"1 hour when young","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"Old-vine Cabernet Franc from clay-limestone that shows how serious Chinon can be: raspberry and red currant edged with violet, graphite and fresh tobacco leaf. Its chalky tannins and savory core need several years in bottle, then it opens into forest floor and dried herbs.","x":"284:2,285:72,286:68,287:50,288:60,289:70,290:72,291:25,292:0,293:25,3:60,6:45,1:45,14:40,13:35,71:50,142:50,140:45,138:35,119:45,88:25,93:30,120:20,151:30,148:20,215:60,214:45,230:45,245:70,242:60,243:65,258:70,278:80,260:55,282:80,279:55,295:100,296:100,310:100,301:100"},{"s":"chateau-de-villeneuve-saumur-champigny","n":"Saumur-Champigny","p":"Château de Villeneuve","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Saumur-Champigny","g":["Cabernet Franc"],"pr":26,"abv":13,"e":"Stainless steel and concrete vats in tufa cellars","sv":"14–16°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–10 years from vintage","ds":"Cabernet Franc from tufa limestone, all fruit and freshness: crunchy raspberry and red cherry with violets and a chalky, cool-toned finish. Silky and juicy, it is best with a light chill on a warm evening.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:50,287:50,288:50,289:62,290:58,291:5,292:0,293:18,3:70,1:55,6:40,9:30,13:30,71:45,138:55,136:30,142:20,119:30,88:20,120:15,229:65,231:45,212:45,215:35,240:85,244:55,236:50,256:60,261:65,279:70,283:50,298:100,296:100,301:100,304:100"},{"s":"catherine-et-pierre-breton-trinch-bourgueil","n":"Trinch! Bourgueil","p":"Catherine & Pierre Breton","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Bourgueil","g":["Cabernet Franc"],"pr":24,"abv":12.5,"e":"Native-yeast fermentation in tank; minimal sulfur","sv":"13–15°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–5 years from vintage","ds":"The name is a toast, and the wine follows suit: tart raspberry, red currant and cranberry with a leafy, peppery Cabernet Franc edge and dusty, light tannins. Organic and minimally handled, it is a chillable bistro red you can drink by the carafe.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:42,287:42,288:38,289:55,290:48,291:0,292:0,293:12,3:60,6:50,1:45,7:30,13:30,71:35,88:30,119:25,120:20,151:25,140:20,229:75,228:40,217:35,240:85,256:85,253:20,242:35,265:75,261:60,279:85,283:80,301:100,298:100,302:100,314:100"},{"s":"domaine-des-baumard-coteaux-du-layon-carte-d-or","n":"Coteaux du Layon Carte d''Or","p":"Domaine des Baumard","t":"dessert","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Coteaux du Layon","g":["Chenin Blanc"],"pr":32,"abv":12.5,"e":"Late-harvested with partial botrytis; fermented and aged in stainless steel","sv":"8–10°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–15 years from vintage","ds":"Sweet Chenin from the schist slopes of Anjou: quince, ripe apricot and yellow peach in a light coating of honey and acacia blossom. Lighter on its feet than Sauternes, its Loire acidity keeps the sweetness juicy and fresh.","x":"284:65,285:80,286:2,287:40,288:62,289:72,290:70,291:0,292:0,293:18,51:65,55:60,54:45,49:35,58:35,43:30,31:30,192:70,209:45,73:35,74:35,79:25,129:15,139:30,229:55,223:35,224:40,240:60,250:55,257:45,270:85,269:50,261:60,279:60,282:60,317:100,320:100,322:100,308:100"},{"s":"henry-marionnet-domaine-de-la-charmoise-touraine-sauvignon","n":"Domaine de la Charmoise Touraine Sauvignon","p":"Henry Marionnet","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Loire Valley","a":"Touraine","g":["Sauvignon Blanc"],"pr":16,"abv":12.5,"e":"Stainless steel; bottled early to preserve freshness","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Within 2–3 years of release","ds":"Pure, exuberant Touraine Sauvignon: gooseberry, grapefruit and lime with a burst of passion fruit and freshly mown grass. Brisk, aromatic and unoaked, it offers much of Sancerre''s charm at half the price.","x":"284:2,285:78,286:1,287:42,288:35,289:62,290:48,291:0,292:0,293:10,66:65,36:60,35:55,60:35,46:40,67:25,89:60,88:25,76:35,94:30,95:20,136:25,137:15,228:80,229:50,225:30,240:95,244:55,256:80,261:90,279:90,283:80,318:100,313:100,305:100,323:100"},{"s":"louis-michel-chablis","n":"Chablis","p":"Domaine Louis Michel & Fils","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Chablis","g":["Chardonnay"],"pr":30,"abv":12.5,"e":"Fermented and aged in stainless steel on fine lees; no oak","sv":"9–11°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–6 years","ds":"Chablis with nothing between you and the Kimmeridgian: lemon, green apple and a cold tang of crushed oyster shell. Steel-raised and lean as a blade, it finishes chalky and saline, the benchmark for what the village tastes like unadorned.","x":"284:2,285:85,286:2,287:40,288:38,289:55,290:62,291:0,292:0,293:15,34:75,46:70,40:45,45:30,49:25,85:30,116:12,144:80,138:85,136:60,141:55,137:25,228:75,225:55,230:55,249:80,243:90,240:85,258:75,261:95,266:25,279:75,283:50,306:100,305:100,303:100,318:100"},{"s":"joseph-drouhin-laforet-bourgogne-pinot-noir","n":"Laforêt Bourgogne Pinot Noir","p":"Joseph Drouhin","t":"red","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Bourgogne","g":["Pinot Noir"],"pr":18,"abv":12.5,"e":"Aged several months mostly in tank, with a portion in older oak","sv":"13–15°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–4 years","ds":"An honest, everyday introduction to red Burgundy: bright cherry and raspberry, a whisper of rose and damp earth, and the juicy lift of cool-climate Pinot. Light on its feet and built for the table rather than the cellar.","x":"284:2,285:62,286:32,287:40,288:38,289:50,290:45,291:12,292:0,293:12,1:80,3:60,4:50,7:30,9:25,72:20,71:12,148:20,151:15,135:12,114:12,212:50,229:65,231:50,240:75,244:65,256:85,258:45,260:35,279:80,283:90,298:100,304:100,301:100,310:100"},{"s":"a-et-p-de-villaine-bouzeron","n":"Bouzeron","p":"A. et P. de Villaine","t":"white","c":"France","r":"Burgundy","a":"Bouzeron","g":["Aligoté"],"pr":33,"abv":12.5,"e":"Fermented and aged in large old foudres and tank; organically farmed old-vine Aligoté Doré","sv":"9–11°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–8 years","ds":"The wine that rescued Aligoté''s reputation: old-vine Aligoté Doré from the Côte Chalonnaise, tasting of lemon, green apple and chamomile over wet stone. Its acidity is bracing, but there is a saline, faintly phenolic texture that gives it far more substance than the grape''s reputation suggests.","x":"284:2,285:85,286:3,287:42,288:42,289:55,290:60,291:10,292:0,293:15,34:65,46:60,47:30,49:30,40:45,45:35,85:35,73:20,79:15,116:25,136:65,138:50,141:40,228:70,230:55,232:20,240:85,249:60,243:70,242:25,260:50,278:45,265:30,279:70,283:55,306:100,318:100,305:100,313:100,323:100"}]'::jsonb);
